{"id": 34, "ts": 1780427642.0014727, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s clarification that Candidate\u202fC creates a positive atmosphere with his crew, which does give him a clear edge on crew cooperation. However, the same feedback also confirms his difficulty communicating ideas, and we already know he is regarded as egocentric and not eager to pursue further education\u2014traits that could undermine cockpit communication and continuous learning, both critical for long\u2011distance operations.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB has demonstrated strong stress resilience (\u201chandles stress very well\u201d) and is very conscientious, indicating reliable, consistent performance under pressure. While he can sometimes adopt the wrong tone, his overall professionalism and technical aptitude (excellent computer skills, good weather assessment) appear more balanced than C\u2019s communication weakness.\nGiven that effective, clear communication and a willingness to develop are non\u2011negotiable for safety\u2011critical flights, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the stronger overall fit."}
